Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,I am writing this from\Na library computer,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.42,0:00:04.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,and I think I am being\Nwatched
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.15,0:00:06.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,from the dark between\Nthe shelves.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.41,0:00:08.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,I know how that\Nsounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.10,0:00:10.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,My best friend trusted\Nthe wrong
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.06,0:00:11.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,person, and now he is\Ngone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.01,0:00:14.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,Let me take you back\Nto the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.18,0:00:16.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,Last year I met a guy\Nnamed Jack.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.73,0:00:18.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,We liked the same\Ngames and the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.62,0:00:20.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,same films, and we\Nplayed
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.15,0:00:22.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,online almost every\Nnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.04,0:00:23.91,Cap,,0,0,0,,For the first time at\Nthat school
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.93,0:00:25.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,I had a real friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.38,0:00:27.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then, last winter, he\Nstarted seeing
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.67,0:00:30.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,a girl from class\Nnamed Elisa.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.02,0:00:31.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,At first she seemed\Nkind.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.88,0:00:34.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,But a month in, Jack\Nbegan to pull away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.59,0:00:36.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,He stopped answering,\Nand he
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.17,0:00:37.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,only wanted to be with\Nher.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.98,0:00:40.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,One morning in the\Ncafeteria line he
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.14,0:00:42.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,turned on me, shouted\Nat a stranger,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.29,0:00:44.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,and ran out of the\Nbuilding.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.27,0:00:46.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,That was not my\Nfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.07,0:00:47.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,He stopped coming to\Nclass.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.87,0:00:49.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,One evening I passed\NElisa in the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.01,0:00:52.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,hall and asked if Jack\Nwas okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.38,0:00:54.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,She smiled, and the\Nsmile was wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.71,0:00:57.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,She said he was better\Nthan ever, each word
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.15,0:00:59.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,slow, like a warning,\Nand walked away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.76,0:01:01.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,That night I called\Nhim.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.44,0:01:02.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,He picked up at once,\Nhis
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.90,0:01:04.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,voice low and shaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.49,0:01:06.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,Forty minutes later he\Nwas at my door,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.79,0:01:09.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,and I knew something\Nwas badly wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.34,0:01:10.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,I let him in and\Nturned off the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.01,0:01:12.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,lights because he\Nbegged me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.97,0:01:14.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the dark he was\Ncrying, but
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.76,0:01:16.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,the tears were black,\Nlike
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.32,0:01:18.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,ink running down his\Nface.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.32,0:01:20.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,He said Elisa did this\Nto him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.54,0:01:22.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,She caught him crying\Nthe black
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.23,0:01:24.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,stuff and said he was\Nready.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.06,0:01:25.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then a soft knock came\Nat the door,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.00,0:01:27.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,and her calm voice\Nsaid it was
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.66,0:01:29.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,time, that they were\Nwaiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.57,0:01:30.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,Jack ran out the back\Nand
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.96,0:01:32.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,vanished into the\Nwoods.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.74,0:01:34.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,I called the police\Nand chased him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.94,0:01:36.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,Something hit the back\Nof my head,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.98,0:01:38.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,and I woke tied to a\Ntree.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.84,0:01:40.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,My mouth was taped\Nshut.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.53,0:01:42.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,In a clearing stood a\Nring of figures
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.69,0:01:45.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,in black robes and\Npale blue masks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.03,0:01:46.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the middle,\Nstrapped
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.25,0:01:47.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,to a chair, was Jack.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.66,0:01:49.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,One lifted her mask.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.25,0:01:50.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,It was Elisa.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.70,0:01:53.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,A taller one read from\Nan old black book.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.49,0:01:55.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,The ground shook, and\Nblack tendrils rose
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.67,0:01:57.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,from the frost and\Nwrapped the chair.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.94,0:02:00.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,They pressed a cracked\Nblue mask over
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.25,0:02:02.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,Jack's face, and where\Nhis eyes
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.19,0:02:04.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,had been, only black\Ntar ran down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.76,0:02:06.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then I heard sirens.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.34,0:02:07.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,The reading stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.71,0:02:09.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,A low laugh came from\Nthe chair, and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.78,0:02:11.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,the thing wearing my\Nfriend tore
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.62,0:02:13.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,free and turned on the\Ncircle.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.65,0:02:15.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,The frost went red.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.14,0:02:16.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,One by one, the robed\Nfigures
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.83,0:02:18.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,stopped screaming, and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.11,0:02:19.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,the clearing went\Nstill.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.96,0:02:21.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,I woke to a flashlight\Nand an
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.73,0:02:23.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,officer shouting for\Nhelp.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.62,0:02:25.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,At the hospital they\Nsaid I would
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.54,0:02:27.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,live, but a kidney was\Ngone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.48,0:02:30.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,A year later, Jack is\Nstill missing, blamed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.04,0:02:32.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,for ten deaths and one\Nattempted murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.73,0:02:33.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,Mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.73,0:02:35.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is inspired by\Nthe story
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.61,0:02:37.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,You Can't Trust\NEveryone, from
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.55,0:02:39.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,an online horror story\Npage.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.82,0:02:40.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,So tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.01,0:02:42.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,Who would you have\Ntrusted?
